## SECTION 10 — Scalability Assessment

**Current hard limits:**
- DB pool: 10 connections max — collapses under ~50 concurrent users
- No pagination on any list endpoint — `getInvoices` returns the entire invoice history
- In-memory filtering (AP routes: status, vendor, date, search all filtered in JS after full table fetch)
- No caching — dashboard summary runs 10 parallel DB queries on every page load
- Report queries are unbounded: Trial Balance runs 6 UNIONs with no date filter
- No job queue — recurring billing, email delivery are synchronous (or non-existent)

**Scaling roadmap required:**
1. Pagination (cursor-based) on all list endpoints — before 500 orgs
2. Redis for dashboard/report caching (5-minute TTL) — before 200 concurrent users
3. DB pool: raise to 50 + PgBouncer — before 1,000 orgs
4. Read replicas for all report queries — before 5,000 orgs
5. Background job queue (BullMQ/Temporal) for recurring billing — required for feature correctness
6. Horizontal Express scaling (PM2 cluster → Kubernetes) — before 10,000 orgs

